%I A398518 #8 Aug 03 2026 03:08:37
%S A398518 1,2,3,4,10,6,42,16,36,60,660,24,312,336,1260,960,8160,432,8208,480,
%T A398518 5040,110880,2550240,1152,14400,74880,505440,120960,3507840,60480,
%U A398518 1874880,92160,760320,12925440,226195200,725760,26853120,27578880,537788160,8985600,368409600,2903040
%N A398518 a(n) = Product_{k=1..n} M(floor(n/k)), where M = A014963 is the exponential Mangoldt function.
%H A398518 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398518/b398518.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A398518 Olivier Bordellès, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/S1793042122501056">On certain sums of number theory</a>, International Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 18, No. 9  (2022), pp. 2053-2074; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.05751v2">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2009.05751 [math.NT], 2020.
%H A398518 Jiamin Li and Jing Ma, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indag.2023.04.001">Three-dimensional exponential sums under constant perturbation</a>, Indagationes Mathematicae, Vol. 34, No. 6 (2023), pp. 1223-1236; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.05870">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2302.05870 [math.NT], 2023.
%H A398518 Kui Liu, Jie Wu, and Zhishan Yang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indag.2021.09.005">A variant of the prime number theorem</a>, Indagationes Mathematicae, Vol. 33, No. 2 (2022), pp. 388-396.
%H A398518 Jing Ma and Jie Wu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10998-020-00359-6">On a sum involving the Mangoldt function</a>, Periodica Mathematica Hungarica, Vol. 83, No. 1 (2021), pp. 39-48.
%H A398518 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/MangoldtFunction.html">Mangoldt Function</a>.
%H A398518 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Von_Mangoldt_function">Von Mangoldt function</a>.
%H A398518 Wei Zhang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnt.2023.10.011">On a variant of the prime number theorem</a>, Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 257 (2024), pp. 163-185; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.12347">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2303.12347 [math.NT], 2023.
%H A398518 Guang-Liang Zhou and Ya-Fang Feng, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1216/rmj.2024.54.623">Distribution of the Primes Represented by floor(x/n) in Short Intervals</a>, Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics, Vol. 54, No. 2 (2024), pp. 623-629.
%F A398518 log(a(n)) = c * n + O(n^(35/71 + eps)), for any eps > 0, where c = 0.449844... = A398519 (Ma and Sun, 2021).
%F A398518 The exponent in the error term was further improved to 97/203 + eps (Bordellès, 2022), 9/19 + eps (Liu et al., 2022), 17/36 + eps (Li and Ma, 2023), and 92/195 + eps (Zhang, 2024).
%t A398518 a[n_] := Product[Exp[MangoldtLambda[Floor[n/k]]], {k, 1, n}]; Array[a, 42]
%o A398518 (PARI) M(n) = if(isprimepower(n, &p), p, 1);
%o A398518 a(n) = prod(k = 1, n, M(n\k));
%Y A398518 Cf. A014963, A398519.
%K A398518 nonn,easy,new
%O A398518 1,2
%A A398518 _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 01 2026
